      "value": 100,
      "dataType": "float",
      "notes": "PlayerSanity.SetInsanity, first of two store sites. Unlike ChangeSanity (a delta), SetInsanity(int) is an ABSOLUTE assignment: clamp(float(arg),0,100) written straight to +0x30, bypassing every other patch in one call. This is the most likely explanation for sanity getting stuck low despite the other patches: whatever calls SetInsanity(0) (a curse/event -- caller not yet identified) can zero it in one shot, and it only recovers once SanityDrainer's per-frame call reaches the already-patched ChangeSanity site again."
    },
